      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from a Native American word meaning “rising sun” or “resting place,” reflecting its quiet, sun‑drenched character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridasmart.com/city-guide/wahneta",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wahneta’s historic citrus packing sheds along Rifle Range Road still stand, weathered but silent testaments to the industry that sustained families.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wahnetawinterhavenneighborhood.org/wahneta-exploring-the-rich-history-and-heartfelt-heritage-of-a-winter-haven-gem/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "First Baptist Church of Wahneta, founded in the mid‑20th century, remains a long‑standing faith institution in the tight‑knit community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wahnetawinterhavenneighborhood.org/wahneta-exploring-the-rich-history-and-heartfelt-heritage-of-a-winter-haven-gem/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wahneta Park, a small green space off Rifle Range Road, hosts family picnics, youth sports, and neighborhood events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wahnetawinterhavenneighborhood.org/wahneta-exploring-the-rich-history-and-heartfelt-heritage-of-a-winter-haven-gem/",
      "category": "landmark",
